{"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to build and run the Swift Package Registry Service.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/app\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Getting started","modules":[{"name":"App"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/App\/documentation\/App"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/App\/documentation\/App\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Github-Personal-Access-Token","text":"Github Personal Access Token"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Many methods of the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.github.com\/en\/rest?apiVersion=2022-11-28","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is accessible without authentication.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.github.com\/en\/rest\/using-the-rest-api\/rate-limits-for-the-rest-api?apiVersion=2022-11-28","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are much lower. Therefore, it is advisable to provide the service with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.github.com\/en\/authentication\/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure\/managing-your-personal-access-tokens","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to authenticate with the Github API."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Building-and-running-migrations","text":"Building and running migrations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check out the repo and do an initial build using the "},{"code":"swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" command line:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["git clone https:\/\/github.com\/CrowdStrike\/swift-package-registry-service.git","cd swift-package-registry-service","swift build"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let’s set up the database which is used for parts of the disk cache:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["swift run App migrate"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You should see something like:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["$ swift run App migrate","...","Build of product 'App' complete! (85.77s)","Migrate Command: Prepare","The following migration(s) will be prepared:","+ App.CreateRepositories on <default>","+ App.CreateManifests on <default>","+ App.CreatePackageReleases on <default>","Would you like to continue?","y\/n> "]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type ‘y’ and then hit Return. Then you should see:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["y\/n> y","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Starting prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreateRepositories]","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Finished prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreateRepositories]","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Starting prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreateManifests]","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Finished prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreateManifests]","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Starting prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreatePackageReleases]","[ INFO ] [Migrator] Finished prepare [database-id: sqlite, migration: App.CreatePackageReleases]","Migration successful"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now you should see a directory created called ","type":"text"},{"code":".sprsCache","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.sqlite","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file inside that directory:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["$ ls -l .sprsCache","total 88","-rw-r--r--  1 ehyche  staff  45056 Jul  1 16:48 db.sqlite","drwxr-xr-x  2 ehyche  staff     64 Jul  1 16:47 manifests","drwxr-xr-x  2 ehyche  staff     64 Jul  1 16:47 sourceArchives"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Running-the-service-from-the-command-line","text":"Running the service from the command line"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now that you have created the disk cache database, then you are now ready to run the service:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["$ export GITHUB_API_TOKEN=\"<your-Github-PAT>\"","$ swift run App serve","Building for debugging...","...","Build of product 'App' complete! (25.07s)","[ NOTICE ] Server started on http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8080"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Testing-the-service-using-curl","text":"Testing the service using curl"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before you point Swift Package Manager at this service, you might want to do some simple curl’s to see it run."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"All of the examples below use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/pointfreeco\/swift-clocks","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an example."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sections below give examples of each of the 5 endpoints of the service. To make it easier, there are scripts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<repo-root>\/scripts"},{"type":"text","text":" directory which take care of all of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"curl"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments. So all of the examples"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"below assume you are in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<repo-root>"},{"type":"text","text":" directory."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"List-Package-Releases","text":"List Package Releases"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["$ .\/scripts\/pr-list-package-releases.sh pointfreeco swift-clocks","{","  \"releases\" : {","    \"0.1.0\" : {","      \"url\" : \"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8080\/pointfreeco\/swift-clocks\/0.1.0\"","    },","    \"